Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 15:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] phy: sun4i-usb: skip squelch detection for VCBUS

VCBUS PHYs do not expose the legacy squelch-detect test-point field.
Pretending this operation is valid for all devices may lead to undefined
behavior.

Make sun4i_usb_phy_set_squelch_detect() a no-op for VCBUS PHYs.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
@@ -643,5 +643,9 @@ void sun4i_usb_phy_set_squelch_detect(struct phy *_phy, bool enabled)
 {
 	struct sun4i_usb_phy *phy = phy_get_drvdata(_phy);
+	struct sun4i_usb_phy_data *data = to_sun4i_usb_phy_data(phy);
+
+	if (data->cfg->vcbus)
+		return;
 
 	sun4i_usb_phy_write(phy, PHY_SQUELCH_DETECT, enabled ? 0 : 2, 2);
 }
